# Phase 4 D-04 — TTS body sway via head IN injection
# Target: Open-LLM-VTuber-Web/src/renderer/WebSDK/src/lappmodel.ts
# Replaces: the earlier body-bob extension that wrote ParamBodyAngleY
# (futile — physics fully overwrites that param every frame).
#
# Root cause discovered via .physics3.json + cubismphysics.ts inspection:
#
#   1. The Teto rig's physics3.json outputs to ParamBodyAngleX/Y/Z with
#      Weight=100. The Cubism physics SDK (cubismphysics.ts:1260-1262)
#      treats Weight>=1.0 as a FULL OVERWRITE: parameterValue[0] = value.
#   2. So ANY motion, body-bob, or direct write to those source body
#      params is silently discarded each frame when physics evaluates.
#   3. The only entry point physics PROPAGATES FROM is the head IN
#      twins (ParamAngleXIN/YIN/ZIN) — physics setting #8 reads them
#      and chains through ParamBodyXINF/YINF/ZINF to the body sway.
#   4. The Option A VTube routing pass clobbers the head IN twins every
#      frame from cursor input, so motion can't write them either.
#
# Fix: inject a small sinusoid into the head IN twins AFTER routing and
# BEFORE physics. ADD (not set) so cursor's value still dominates; the
# sway adds a small wobble on top, which physics propagates through the
# rig's chain to produce visible body sway during TTS.
#
# Insertion point: lappmodel.ts update(), replacing the old body-bob
# block (right after the watermark force-pin, before the original
# cursor drag adds).
#
# Field declaration unchanged from prior body-bob patch:
#   _speechRmsSmoothed: number;
# Initialized in constructor:
#   this._speechRmsSmoothed = 0;
#
# New block (replaces old body-bob block):
#
#   if (this._lipsync && this._wavFileHandler) {
#     const rms = Math.min(1.0, this._wavFileHandler.getRms() * 1.5);
#     this._speechRmsSmoothed = this._speechRmsSmoothed * 0.85 + rms * 0.15;
#     if (this._speechRmsSmoothed > 0.005) {
#       const t = this._userTimeSeconds;
#       this._model.addParameterValueById(
#         CubismFramework.getIdManager().getId("ParamAngleXIN"),
#         Math.sin(t * 0.7) * 5.0 * this._speechRmsSmoothed
#       );
#       this._model.addParameterValueById(
#         CubismFramework.getIdManager().getId("ParamAngleZIN"),
#         Math.sin(t * 0.4 + 1.3) * 3.0 * this._speechRmsSmoothed
#       );
#     }
#   }
#
# Tuning notes:
#   - 5° X amplitude + 3° Z amplitude scaled by smoothed RMS gives a
#     gentle wobble during typical speech. Phase offset on Z (+1.3 rad)
#     prevents X and Z syncing into a flat repetitive arc.
#   - 0.7 / 0.4 rad·s frequencies → ~0.9 / ~0.5 Hz, slow enough to read
#     as natural body settling, fast enough to feel alive.
#   - RMS gate at 0.005 stops the sway during silence between sentences.
#   - Talk1.motion3.json / Talk2.motion3.json remain in the rig data but
#     are effectively no-ops (they target *IN body twins which are
#     orphaned in this rig). Future work: remove them from the model3.json
#     Talk group, or repurpose for facial-expression timing if needed.
